aro</strong> (the anime hamster!), <strong>Nibbles</strong>, <strong>Peanut</strong>, <strong>Gizmo</strong>, <strong>Cheeks</strong>, <strong>Biscuit</strong>, <strong>Squishy</strong>.\"}}]\n26:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Food names work wonderfully for hamsters: <strong>Mochi</strong>, <strong>Waffles</strong>, <strong>Tofu</strong>, <strong>Nugget</strong>, <strong>Dumpling</strong>, <strong>Pancake</strong>, <strong>Popcorn</strong>, <strong>Noodle</strong>. Action names for their endless energy: <strong>Turbo</strong>, <strong>Zoom</strong>, <strong>Bolt</strong>, <strong>Scooter</strong>, <strong>Dash</strong>, <strong>Flash</strong>, <strong>Rocket</strong>. Celebrity hamsters: <strong>Beyoncé</strong>, <strong>Ham Solo</strong>, <strong>Chewbacca</strong>, <strong>Hamlet</strong>.\"}}]\n27:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Guinea Pig Names 🐹\"]}]\n28:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Guinea pigs are vocal, social, and endlessly expressive. Their distinctive 'wheek' sounds and popcorning jumps deserve names full of personality. Popular guinea pig names: <strong>Pippin</strong>, <strong>Willow</strong>, <strong>Daisy</strong>, <strong>Oreo</strong>, <strong>Ginger</strong>, <strong>Cocoa</strong>, <strong>Patches</strong>.\"}}]\n29:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Guinea pigs often come in pairs or groups, making themed names especially fun. Royal pairs: <strong>Victoria & Albert</strong>, <strong>Will & Kate</strong>, <strong>Cleopatra & Caesar</strong>. Food pairs: <strong>Peanut & Butter</strong>, <strong>Coffee & Cream</strong>, <strong>Mac & Cheese</strong>, <strong>Cookie & Cream</strong>. Literary pairs: <strong>Frodo & Sam</strong>, <strong>Sherlock & Watson</strong>, <strong>Romeo & Juliet</strong>.\"}}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Mouse & Rat Names 🐭\"]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Mice and rats are among the most intelligent small pets, capable of learning tricks and forming deep bonds with owners. Famous mouse names: <strong>Mickey</strong>, <strong>Minnie</strong>, <strong>Stuart Little</strong>, <strong>Fievel</strong>, <strong>Jerry</strong>, <strong>Gus Gus</strong>, <strong>Despereaux</strong>, <strong>Remy</strong> (from Ratatouille!).\"}}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Rats deserve names that honor their intelligence: <strong>Einstein</strong>, <strong>Tesla</strong>, <strong>Newton</strong>, <strong>Darwin</strong>, <strong>Curie</strong>, <strong>Sagan</strong>. Their long tails and agility inspire: <strong>Spaghetti</strong>, <strong>Noodle</strong>, <strong>Slinky</strong>, <strong>Rope</strong>. Movie rat names: <strong>Splinter</strong> (TMNT), <strong>Templeton</strong> (Charlotte's Web), <strong>Rizzo</strong> (Muppets).\"}}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Gerbil & Other Small Pet Names 🐿️\"]}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Gerbils, degus, chinchillas, and other small rodents each have unique charms. Gerbils: <strong>Sandy</strong>, <strong>Dune</strong>, <strong>Desert</strong>, <strong>Digger</strong>, <strong>Tunnels</strong>. Their desert origins inspire: <strong>Sahara</strong>, <strong>Gobi</strong>, <strong>Oasis</strong>. For degus: <strong>Squirrel</strong>, <strong>Acorn</strong>, <strong>Nutkin</strong>.\"}}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"For {chinchilla}s: <strong>Velvet</strong>, <strong>Cashmere</strong>, <strong>Dusty</strong> (for their dust baths!), <strong>Puff</strong>, <strong>Silver</strong>, <strong>Plush</strong>. They're prized for their incredibly soft fur, so luxury names fit: <strong>Chanel</strong>, <strong>Prada</strong>, <strong>Gucci</strong>, <strong>Cashmere</strong>, <strong>Satin</strong>.\"}}]\n30:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Names for Pairs & Groups 👥\"]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Since many small pets thrive in pairs, themed duo names are especially popular. Dynamic duos: <strong>Batman & Robin</strong>, <strong>Mario & Luigi</strong>, <strong>Anna & Elsa</strong>, <strong>Woody & Buzz</strong>, <strong>Lilo & Stitch</strong>. Complementary pairs: <strong>Salt & Pepper</strong>, <strong>Thunder & Lightning</strong>, <strong>Sunny & Stormy</strong>, <strong>Yin & Yang</strong>.\"}}]\n32:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Group names for trios or colonies: The Spice Girls (<strong>Ginger, Posh, Baby, Scary, Sporty</strong>), The Seven Dwarfs, The Avengers. Musical groups: <strong>Freddie, Brian, John, Roger</strong> (Queen), <strong>John, Paul, George, Ringo</strong> (Beatles).\"}}]\n33:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Should I give my small pet a human name or a pet name?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Both work wonderfully. Human names like Kevin or Susan on tiny pets create delightful humor. Pet-style names like Nibbles or Peanut feel instinctively right. Follow your heart — there are no rules!\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do I name multiple small pets that look alike?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Use collar colors, personality differences, or subtle marking differences. If truly identical, give them a collective theme name and refer to them as a group — The Nuggets, The Triplets, The Spice Girls.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Do small pets learn their names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Rats and mice definitely recognize their names with training. Guinea pigs learn the sound of their names, especially associated with food. Hamsters and gerbils are less responsive but still benefit from consistent naming.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What small pet names are trending right now?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Food names dominate small pet naming: Mochi, Tofu, Dumpling, and Nugget are extremely popular. Pop culture names from anime, gaming, and social media also trend heavily.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n34:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"hamster\",{\"href\":\"/animal/hamster/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐹\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Hamster\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"guinea-pig\",{\"href\":\"/animal/guinea-pig/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐹\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Guinea Pig\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"gerbil\",{\"href\":\"/animal/gerbil/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐭\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Gerbil\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"chinchilla\",{\"href\":\"/animal/chinchilla/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐿️\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Chinchilla\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"bushmaster\",{\"href\":\"/animal/bushmaster/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐍\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Bushmaster\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"painted-turtle\",{\"href\":\"/animal/painted-turtle/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐢\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Painted Turtle\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"demoiselle-crane\",{\"href\":\"/animal/demoiselle-crane/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐦\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Demoiselle Crane\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"orca\",{\"href\":\"/animal/orca/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐋\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Orca\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n35:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"📖 Related Naming Guides\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\"