ldren\":[5,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#pairs\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Names for Pairs & Groups\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[6,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#faq\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}]]}]]}]]}],\"$La\",\"$Lb\",\"$Lc\",\"$Ld\",\"$Le\",\"$Lf\",\"$L10\",\"$L11\",\"$L12\",\"$L13\",\"$L14\",\"$L15\",\"$L16\",\"$L17\",\"$L18\",\"$L19\"]}],\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\",\"$L1c\",\"$L1d\",\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\"]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$21\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@22\"}]}]\na:[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Small pets have enormous personalities packed into tiny bodies. A \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"66\",{\"href\":\"/animal/hamster/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Hamster\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"77\",{\"href\":\"/animal/guinea-pig/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Guinea Pig\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"91\",{\"href\":\"/animal/gerbil/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Gerbil\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", mouse, or rat may be small in stature, but they deserve names as big as their hearts. This guide celebrates the art of naming the smallest members of our animal families.\"]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Hamster Names 🐹\"]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Hamsters are the clowns of the small pet world — always stuffing cheeks, running wheels at 3 AM, and escaping in the most dramatic ways. Their names should match their chaotic energy. Classic hamster names: <strong>Hamtaro</strong> (the anime hamster!), <strong>Nibbles</strong>, <strong>Peanut</strong>, <strong>Gizmo</strong>, <strong>Cheeks</strong>, <strong>Biscuit</strong>, <strong>Squishy</strong>.\"}}]\nd:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Food names work wonderfully for hamsters: <strong>Mochi</strong>, <strong>Waffles</strong>, <strong>Tofu</strong>, <strong>Nugget</strong>, <strong>Dumpling</strong>, <strong>Pancake</strong>, <strong>Popcorn</strong>, <strong>Noodle</strong>. Action names for their endless energy: <strong>Turbo</strong>, <strong>Zoom</strong>, <strong>Bolt</strong>, <strong>Scooter</strong>, <strong>Dash</strong>, <strong>Flash</strong>, <strong>Rocket</strong>. Celebrity hamsters: <strong>Beyoncé</strong>, <strong>Ham Solo</strong>, <strong>Chewbacca</strong>, <strong>Hamlet</strong>.\"}}]\ne:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Guinea Pig Names 🐹\"]}]\nf:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Guinea pigs are vocal, social, and endlessly expressive. Their distinctive 'wheek' sounds and popcorning jumps deserve names full of personality. Popular guinea pig names: <strong>Pippin</strong>, <strong>Willow</strong>, <strong>Daisy</strong>, <strong>Oreo</strong>, <strong>Ginger</strong>, <strong>Cocoa</strong>, <strong>Patches</strong>.\"}}]\n10:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Guinea pigs often come in pairs or groups, making themed names especially fun. Royal pairs: <strong>Victoria & Albert</strong>, <strong>Will & Kate</strong>, <strong>Cleopatra & Caesar</strong>. Food pairs: <strong>Peanut & Butter</strong>, <strong>Coffee & Cream</strong>, <strong>Mac & Cheese</strong>, <strong>Cookie & Cream</strong>. Literary pairs: <strong>Frodo & Sam</strong>, <strong>Sherlock & Watson</strong>, <strong>Romeo & Juliet</strong>.\"}}]\n11:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Mouse & Rat Names 🐭\"]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Mice and rats are among the most intelligent small pets, capable of learning tricks and forming deep bonds with owners. Famous mouse names: <strong>Mickey</strong>, <strong>Minnie</strong>, <strong>Stuart Little</strong>, <strong>Fievel</strong>, <strong>Jerry</strong>, <strong>Gus Gus</strong>, <strong>Despereaux</strong>, <strong>Remy</strong> (from Ratatouille!).\"}}]\n13:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Rats deserve names that honor their intelligence: <strong>Einstein</strong>, <strong>Tesla</strong>, <strong>Newton</strong>, <strong>Darwin</strong>, <strong>Curie</strong>, <strong>Sagan</strong>. Their long tails and agility inspire: <strong>Spaghetti</strong>, <strong>Noodle</strong>, <strong>Slinky</strong>, <strong>Rope</strong>. Movie rat names: <strong>Splinter</strong> (TMNT), <strong>Templeton</strong> (Charlotte's Web), <strong>Rizzo</strong> (Muppets).\"}}]\n14:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Gerbil & Other Small Pet Names 🐿️\"]}]\n15:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Gerbils, degus, chinchillas, and other small rodents each have unique charms. Gerbils: <strong>Sandy</strong>, <strong>Dune</strong>, <strong>Desert</strong>, <strong>Digger</strong>, <strong>Tunnels</strong>. Their desert origins inspire: <strong>Sahara</strong>, <strong>Gobi</strong>, <strong>Oasis</strong>. For degus: <strong>Squirrel</strong>, <strong>Acorn</strong>, <strong>Nutkin</strong>.\"}}]\n16:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"For {chinchilla}s: <strong>Velvet</strong>, <strong>Cashmere</strong>, <strong>Dusty</strong> (for their dust baths!), <strong>Puff</strong>, <strong>Silver</strong>, <strong>Plush</strong>. They're prized for their incredibly soft fur, so luxury names fit: <strong>Chanel</strong>, <strong>Prada</strong>, <strong>Gucci</strong>, <strong>Cashmere</strong>, <strong>Satin</strong>.\"}}]\n17:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Names for Pairs & Groups 👥\"]}]\n18:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Since many small pets thrive in pairs, themed duo names are especially popular. Dynamic duos: <strong>Batman & Robin</strong>, <strong>Mario & Luigi</strong>, <strong>Anna & Elsa</strong>, <strong>Woody & Buzz</strong>, <strong>Lilo & Stitch</strong>. Complementary pairs: <strong>Salt & Pepper</strong>, <strong>Thunder & Lightning</strong>, <strong>Sunny & Stormy</strong>, <strong>Yin & Yang</strong>.\"}}]\n19:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Group names for trios or colonies: The Spice Girls (<strong>Ginger, Posh, Baby, Scary, Sporty</strong>), The Seven Dwarfs, The Avengers. Musical groups: <strong>Freddie, Brian, John, Roger</strong> (Queen), <strong>John, Paul, George, Ringo</strong> (Beatles).\"}}]\n1a:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",